            <abstract>
                <gco:CharacterString>This project captured high resolution elevation data using LiDAR technology covering over the greater Brisbane area, extending southwest to Laidley, north to Murrumba Downs, south to Springwood, and extending slightly into the D’Aguilar Range to the village of Mt Glorious.&#13;
No imagery was captured for this project, The size of AOI for this project was 3306.2 square kilometre. &#13;
Copy this URL into your browser to order and download individual data tiles in GeoTIFF and LAS format - https://elevation.fsdf.org.au/?maxx=153.212664&amp;maxy=-27.266905&amp;minx=152.645994&amp;miny=-27.664149&amp;metadata=E5EAAFE5-3EDA-4FC6-B41E-78237CDEC0BE</gco:CharacterString>
            </abstract>
            <purpose>
                <gco:CharacterString>To provide highly accurate elevation data for use in risk assessment, the management of natural disasters, infrastructure planning, developing strategies to support climate change, topographic mapping and modelling.</gco:CharacterString>
            </purpose>
